<title>FRANCE: France publishes Aug crude imports, latest margins.</title>
<headline>France publishes Aug crude imports, latest margins.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's industry ministry on Thursday issued the following data for deliveries to refineries.</p>
<p>Crude deliveries are by origin (in thousand tonnes). Total includes modest deliveries from domestic French crude production.</p>
<p>					  Aug 1996   July 1996   Aug 1995</p>
<p>    Total				 6,773	8,095	6,113</p>
<p>    including Saudi Arabia	  1,278	1,677	1,048</p>
<p>		  Iraq			  0	    0	    0</p>
<p>		  Iran			649	1,044	1,207</p>
<p>		  Kuwait			0	  271	  271</p>
<p>		  Algeria		   312	   82	   40</p>
<p>		  Libya		     261	  249	  163</p>
<p>		  Nigeria		   322	1,156	  203</p>
<p>		  Britain		 1,347	1,001	  763</p>
<p>		  Norway		  1,093	1,257	1,018</p>
<p>		  ex-USSR		   784	  811	  594</p>
<p>The ministry also released the following data for French refining margins, based on North Sea Brent crude ($/barrel).</p>
<p>			   Sept 1996  Aug 1996  July 1996  Sept 1995</p>
<p>    Refining Margin     2.65	1.66	2.02	2.09</p>
<p>In the most recent month for which refinery capacity utilisation is available, French plants ran at 92 percent of capacity in August, up from 91 percent in July but down from 94 percent in August 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
